# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MercForge .gitignore — set up 2026-05-22 (local-only repo, may push
# to GitHub later). Source under sidecar/ + frontend/ + shell/ is
# versioned; everything else here is regenerable build output, vendor
# state, or working data that doesn't belong in history.
#
# Sizing context (pre-gitignore tree was ~5.3 GB; after exclusions
# the source-only tree is ~30-50 MB):
#   shell/target/                  4.3 GB  Cargo build cache
#   sidecar/.venv/                 128 MB  Python venv (recreated from requirements.txt)
#   frontend/node_modules/         105 MB  npm deps (recreated from package-lock.json)
#   shell/binaries/                 62 MB  PyInstaller-bundled sidecar .exe
#   sidecar/build/ + sidecar/dist/  56 MB  PyInstaller artifacts
#   frontend/dist/                 481 KB  Vite build output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Python sidecar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
# PyInstaller artifacts
sidecar/build/
sidecar/dist/
sidecar/*.toc
sidecar/*.manifest
# Generic build/ catches stray PyInstaller spec runs anywhere
build/
sdist/
wheels/
eggs/
.eggs/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.installed.cfg

# ── Frontend / Vite / Node ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
coverage/

# ── Rust / Tauri shell ──────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
shell/target/
src-tauri/target/
# Tauri-autogenerated capability/ACL schemas (mirror of the already-ignored
# ja2-launcher/shell/gen/). Regenerated by the Tauri build; no need to commit.
/shell/gen/
# PyInstaller drops the sidecar .exe here for Tauri to bundle. The
# binary is rebuilt by launch_current.ps1; no need to commit.
shell/binaries/

# ── Working data that lives outside the repo now ────────────────────
# Moved 2026-05-22 to <wasteland_root>/MercForge_Megapack/ and
# <wasteland_root>/MercForge_Distributables/. These guards catch
# leftovers + any future regressions where someone re-adds the
# folders by accident.
megapack/
/dist/
# `dist/` at root is the bundle output dir; the `/` prefix scopes the
# ignore to the project root so `frontend/dist/` etc. still need
# their own rules above (and they have them).

# ── Distribution artifacts + bundle exports ─────────────────────────
*.msi
# Belt-and-suspenders against a stray installer / packaged build.
*.exe
# .wmerc bundle exports are user-data output. If you want to share
# one as a test fixture, drop it under sidecar/tests/fixtures/.
*.wmerc

# ── Sidecar atomic-write tmp files + per-edit .dat backups ──────────
*.mwtmp
# .bak files are user-data-protection backups (e.g. .dat.bak from
# MapForge edits, Ja2Set.dat.xml.bak from library imports). Don't
# commit but don't blow them away either.
*.bak

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ── IDE / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Local testing scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────
test_install/
scratch/
# Playwright/browser-MCP run artifacts (screenshots, traces) dropped at
# repo root during MapForge GUI smoke tests. Regenerable; not source.
.playwright-mcp/
# Root-level scratch PNGs from MapForge debug captures (e.g.
# scratch_build21_sub21.png, scratch_painter_*.png). The `scratch/`
# rule above only matches a `scratch/` directory; these are loose
# files dropped at repo root by debug helpers.
scratch_*.png

# ── Local environment overrides ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── ja2-launcher sibling subproject build artifacts ─────────────────
# ja2-launcher is a standalone Tauri+React app sitting in this repo
# (designed to eventually fold into MercForge). Its source is tracked,
# but its build outputs are regenerable and should not be committed.
ja2-launcher/frontend/dist/
ja2-launcher/shell/gen/
# tools/generated_schemas/ is the output dir of build_ini_schemas.py.
# Regenerable from a vanilla Data-1.13 dir.
ja2-launcher/tools/generated_schemas/
